## 👤 **User Story – Slack-Based Device Request Approval Workflow**

### **Title**: Slack Integration for Device Request Approvals

### **As a**

Manager of an associate who requested a device,

### **I want**

to receive an actionable Slack notification with the associate’s request details and Approve/Reject buttons,

### **So that**

I can quickly review the request and approve or reject it in real time without logging into a separate system, while ensuring my response is securely recorded and the workflow advances automatically.

---

### 📘 **Detailed Description**

When an associate submits a request for a new laptop or accessory through the **Storefront platform**, the system initiates an automated Slack notification to the associate’s reporting manager.

This Slack message is sent via the **Virtual Storefront Slack App**, and includes:

* Associate’s name, email, job title, department, and associate ID
* Requested device model and OS
* List of accessories (if applicable)
* Requester's email (if different from the associate)
* Two action buttons: ✅ Approve and ❌ Reject

Upon interaction with the buttons:

* The system **captures the manager’s response** (Approve/Reject)
* The system also **records the exact timestamp** of the interaction (`user_interacted_at`)
* The data is **stored in the `slack_response` table** for traceability and audit logging
* The request then moves to the next workflow stage: provisioning, notification, or closure, depending on the manager’s response

This feature reduces approval delays, eliminates dependency on emails, and offers a modern, chat-based interaction model that integrates seamlessly with Slack.

---

### ✅ **Acceptance Criteria**

| ID  | Scenario             | Given                                 | When                                  | Then                                                                                                |
| --- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| AC1 | Slack Notification   | An associate submits a device request | The request is successfully submitted | The associate’s manager receives a Slack notification                                               |
| AC2 | Slack Message Format | A Slack message is sent               |                                       | It includes associate name, email, job title, department, associate ID, device, OS, and accessories |
| AC3 | Manager Approval     | Manager clicks “Approve”              |                                       | The system records the approval and timestamp, and triggers the next step in the workflow           |
| AC4 | Manager Rejection    | Manager clicks “Reject”               |                                       | The system records the rejection and timestamp, and halts the request                               |
| AC5 | Traceability         | A manager responds                    |                                       | The response and `user_interacted_at` are saved in the `slack_response` table                       |

---

### 📊 **Tracking and Logging**

* All manager interactions are logged with:

  * `request_id`
  * `manager_email`
  * `action_taken` (approve/reject)
  * `user_interacted_at`
* These records will support audit logs, reporting, and future SLA validations.

---

### 🚀 **Business Value**

* Reduces time-to-approve by eliminating portal-based review
* Improves experience for both requesters and managers
* Enables real-time workflows and traceability
* Centralized record of approval events for compliance and audit

